    {
      "content": "For a fixed integer n>1, define F_n(x) = floor(n x) - sum_{k=1}^n floor(k x)/k for every real number x.",
      "kind": "definition",
      "label": "F_n"
    },
    {
      "content": "For a fixed positive integer n, let H_n = sum_{k=1}^n 1/k.",
      "kind": "notation",
      "label": "H_n"
    },
    {
      "content": "For a real number x, let frac(x) = x - floor(x); then frac(x) lies in [0,1).",
      "kind": "notation",
      "label": "frac"
    }
  ],
  "strategy_summary": "Use integer-periodicity to reduce to the fractional part in [0,1), then use piecewise monotonicity on each interval [j/n,(j+1)/n) to reduce to the grid points j/n. The only hard arithmetic input is a discrete harmonic-floor inequality at those grid points. The top interval [(n-1)/n,1) is then checked by direct floor evaluation, giving the exact maximizers and maximum value.",
  "updated_at": "2026-03-28T00:12:49.597515Z"
